# REQUIRES: python-api, openmm, cuda
# The gradients of the energy of a frame in the positions and in the strain
# (D252, docs/python-frames.md) of the whole potential
# against OpenMM, on a GPU, in double and mixed precision,
# Inputs/python_frame_gradients.py: the dipeptide in water with PME at the
# same splitting parameter and grid, a cutoff of 0.8 nm, and the
# Lennard-Jones shifted there. G against OpenMM's forces (its Reference
# platform, in double precision); the nine components of S against central
# differences under the strain of OpenMM's energy less u(r_c) of the pairs
# within the cutoff, since OpenMM reports no virial and cuts without a
# shift. At 64 and 128 points; the tolerance is three times what the two
# programs change by between the grids.
# RUN: %mdir_python %S/Inputs/python_frame_gradients.py %S/Inputs/dipeptide openmm GPU Double | FileCheck %s -DMODE="GPU Double"
# RUN: %mdir_python %S/Inputs/python_frame_gradients.py %S/Inputs/dipeptide openmm GPU Mixed | FileCheck %s -DMODE="GPU Mixed"
# CHECK: [[MODE]]: the dipeptide in water, 1168 particles: G of the whole potential against the forces of OpenMM, grid 64
# CHECK: [[MODE]]: the dipeptide in water: the nine components of S against central differences of the energy of OpenMM, grid 64
# CHECK: [[MODE]]: the dipeptide in water: the same at 128 points, G
# CHECK: [[MODE]]: the dipeptide in water: the same at 128 points, S
# CHECK: openmm passed
